  "body": "### What problem are you trying to solve?\n\nSome of us over in Open UI have been designing the new menu elements proposal ([explainer](https://open-ui.org/components/menu.explainer/)), which is a suite of new HTML elements designed to fulfill the [menu](https://w3c.github.io/aria/#menu) and [menubar](https://w3c.github.io/aria/#menubar) roles / pattern. Please see the [APG pattern](https://www.w3.org/WAI/ARIA/apg/patterns/menubar/) for more details, which served as some initial motivation and inspiration for our proposal.\n\nOur goal is to produce a set of menu primitives with sensible built-in keyboard navigability, accessibility, and activation defaults, as we've observed this pattern widely across the web, with each instance varying slightly in all forms of behavior, and many of which have very poor accessibility characteristics. Our proposal builds off of recent primitives such as popovers and anchor positioning, and all of the design details to date have been collected in the explainer: https://open-ui.org/components/menu.explainer/. Please take a look!\n\nOur goal is eventual inclusion in HTML, so we'd love to propose stage 1, and discuss this at the WHATNOT meeting scheduled for 2025-10-09.\n\n/cc @mfreed7 @josepharhar\n\n### What solutions exist today?\n\n_No response_\n\n### How would you solve it?\n\n_No response_\n\n### Anything else?\n\n_No response_",
